---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import demo from '../../../data/demo-report.json';
---
<Layout title="llms.txt Checker — Free AI Guidance File Audit | GeoScore"
  schema={{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
    name: 'llms.txt Checker',
    description: 'Free online tool to check if your website has an llms.txt file that guides AI models like ChatGPT, Claude, and Perplexity to understand your content.',
    url: 'https://geoscore.help/tools/llms-txt-checker/',
    applicationCategory: 'SEO Tool',
    operatingSystem: 'Any',
    offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
    isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebApplication', name: 'GeoScore', url: 'https://geoscore.help' }
  }}
>
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <div class="text-center mb-10">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-geo-500/10 text-geo-400 border border-geo-500/20 mb-4">
        Free Tool
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold mb-3">llms.txt Checker</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="card p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">How to Check Your llms.txt</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mb-6">Enter your website URL below to run a full GEO audit, including llms.txt analysis:</p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 max-w-xl">
        <div class="flex-1 relative">
          <svg class="absolute left-4 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 w-5 h-5 text-gray-500" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 8v4l3 3"/></svg>
          <input id="url-input" type="url" placeholder="e.g. example.com" aria-label="Enter website URL" onkeydown="if(event.key==='Enter'){document.getElementById('audit-btn').click();}" class="w-full pl-12 pr-5 py-3.5 rounded-xl bg-white/5 text-white placeholder-gray-500 border border-gray-600 focus:border-brand-500 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-brand-500/30 text-lg transition" />
        </div>
        <button id="audit-btn" class="px-8 py-3.5 rounded-xl font-semibold text-white bg-gradient-to-r from-geo-600 to-brand-600 hover:from-geo-500 hover:to-brand-500 transition shadow-lg shadow-brand-500/20 whitespace-nowrap">Check Now</button>
      </div>
    </div>

      <p class="text-gray-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-10 text-center">Check if your website has an <code class="text-geo-400 bg-white/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">llms.txt</code> file that guides AI models like ChatGPT, Claude, and Perplexity to understand your content.</p>

      <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mb-10 text-center">
        <a href="/report/demo/" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-geo-400 transition underline underline-offset-2">See a sample report</a>
        &mdash; {demo.host} scored <span class="text-geo-400 font-semibold">{demo.score}/100 ({demo.level})</span>, {demo.dimensionsAboveSixty}/{demo.dimensionCount} dimensions above 60%. Try your own URL.
      </p>

    <div class="card p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">What is llms.txt?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">
        <code class="text-geo-400 bg-white/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">llms.txt</code> is a proposed standard (similar to robots.txt) that provides AI language models with structured information about your website. It helps AI search engines understand what your site is about, what content to prioritize, and how to cite your pages.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">
        As AI search engines like <strong class="text-white">ChatGPT</strong>, <strong class="text-white">Perplexity</strong>, <strong class="text-white">Claude</strong>, and <strong class="text-white">Google AI Overviews</strong> become mainstream, having a proper llms.txt file is critical for AI visibility.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">llms.txt Best Practices</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-400">
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-geo-500 flex-shrink-0">✓</span><span>Place <code class="text-geo-400 bg-white/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">llms.txt</code> at the root of your domain (e.g., <code class="bg-white/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">https://example.com/llms.txt</code>)</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-geo-500 flex-shrink-0">✓</span><span>Include a brief description of your site or project</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-geo-500 flex-shrink-0">✓</span><span>List key URLs that AI models should prioritize</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-geo-500 flex-shrink-0">✓</span><span>Use Markdown-style formatting for readability</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-geo-500 flex-shrink-0">✓</span><span>Keep it concise — under 2KB is ideal</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-geo-500 flex-shrink-0">✓</span><span>Update it when you add major new content sections</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">What this checker actually verifies</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">
        The audit scores <strong class="text-white">five</strong> things about your <code class="text-geo-400 bg-white/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">llms.txt</code>, not a longer wish list. Being explicit about the boundary matters: a checklist you cannot verify is a checklist you cannot act on.
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-400">
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-geo-500 flex-shrink-0">1</span><span><strong class="text-white">It exists.</strong> Any 200 text response at <code class="bg-white/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">/llms.txt</code> counts — including a soft-404 HTML error page, which is a known limitation of every HTTP-based checker.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-geo-500 flex-shrink-0">2</span><span><strong class="text-white">Structure.</strong> The file must open with an <code class="bg-white/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"># H1</code> and contain a <code class="bg-white/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">&gt; summary</code> line. Both are one check.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-geo-500 flex-shrink-0">3</span><span><strong class="text-white">At least 2 area sections</strong> — <code class="bg-white/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">## Heading</code> lines. <code class="bg-white/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">###</code> does not count.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-geo-500 flex-shrink-0">4</span><span><strong class="text-white">Descriptive links</strong> — at least one absolute <code class="bg-white/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">https://</code> URL in markdown link form. A file whose links are all relative fails this one.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-geo-500 flex-shrink-0">5</span><span><strong class="text-white">Under 200 lines</strong> — and this point only counts once the structure check passes, so an empty file earns nothing for being short.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mt-4 mb-0">
        The best practices above are guidance, not all scored criteria. Publishing an <code class="bg-white/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">llms.txt</code> is a low-cost option, not a proven ranking factor — see <a href="/methodology/" class="text-geo-400 hover:underline">how the score is computed</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Example llms.txt File</h2>
      <pre class="bg-black/30 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm text-gray-300 overflow-x-auto"><code># Example Site

> A brief description of what this website is about.

## Key Pages
- [About Us](https://example.com/about): Company background
- [Products](https://example.com/products): Product catalog
- [Blog](https://example.com/blog): Latest articles
- [Contact](https://example.com/contact): Get in touch

## Optional
- [Privacy Policy](https://example.com/privacy)
- [Terms](https://example.com/terms)</code></pre>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mb-8">
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-semibold text-white bg-gradient-to-r from-geo-600 to-brand-600 hover:from-geo-500 hover:to-brand-500 transition">
        Run Full GEO Audit →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
  (function() {
    var queue = [];
    ["startAudit","showBatchInput","showComparison","startBatchAudit","runComparison","doExport"].forEach(function(n) {
      window[n] = function() { queue.push({ n: n, a: arguments }); };
    });
    window.__geoFlush = function() { queue.splice(0).forEach(function(q) { window[q.n].apply(null, q.a); }); };
  })();
</script>
<script src="../../scripts/boot.js"></script>
